riginal preference (OR=1.65, p=0.072) — is this appropriately handled?\n\n### 4. Presentation of Results\n- Are the tables clear and informative?\n- Any missing figures that would strengthen the paper? (The paper has 9 tables but apparently no figures)\n- Is the narrative well-structured?\n\n## Output Format\nProvide your review in this exact structure:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methodology &amp; Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentence summary of the paper's contribution from your perspective]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, each with a short label and explanation]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, each with a short label and explanation. Be specific about what's missing or problematic.]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list of specific questions you'd want answered]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Bulleted list of minor presentation/clarity issues]\n\n### Scores\n- Methodological Soundness: X/6\n- Experimental Rigor: X/6\n- Statistical Analysis: X/6\n- Clarity: X/6\n- Overall: X/6\n\n### Confidence\n[1-5 scale: 1=low, 5=expert]\n```\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011CDC511Ai1QYqyMYY5zYnf","session_id":"f191c373-9bcf-4685-a04d-b4374a1ca49f","uuid":"707cca20-80a6-4e73-9abf-7394908704e3","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:40:46.864Z"}
